/-!
# Non-vacuity witnesses: exclusive accesses and LSE atomics in `checkObj` (#553)

`checkObj` models `LDAXR*` (an acquire load), `STLXR*` (a store whose status register becomes 0:
the exclusive store succeeds on one core), `CASAL*` (`Ex.eqsel`: the new value is stored on a
match, else the old one, which leaves the memory as it was) and the LSE read-modify-writes
`LDADDAL*`, `LDCLRAL*`, `LDEORAL*`, `LDORAL*`, `SWPAL*` (`rmwEx`), on the word side (`symInsn`'s
`.ldstExcl`, `.cas`, `.atomic` arms, `symRmw`) and on the Prog side (`exclOp`, `atomOp`, `atomP`,
as `progEffect`).

* `objAtomic_prog_witness`: `std/std/sync/atomic/AddInt32,1.prog` of the corpus
  (`gofv-corpus/2aae1000ea1d/quick-v10/plain`, embedded verbatim as `fProg`), run through the
  assembler port as `obj-check` does (`GoFVTest/ObjCheck.lean`, `checkFile`). By compiled
  evaluation (`native_decide`, listed in `scripts/axioms-allowlist.txt`; `atomic_facts`),
  `checkProg` accepts its Progs `LDADDALW R1, (R0), R2`, `LDAXRW (R0), R2` and
  `STLXRW R2, (R0), R27` against their words (`LDADDAL W1, W2, [X0]`, `LDAXR W2, [X0]`,
  `STLXR W27, W2, [X0]`), and `progSym` gives the effects `σAdd` (the old value to `R2`, the sum
  stored) and `σStx` (the store, `R27` 0); only `STLXRW` leaves `X27` related (`est27`).
* `objAtomic_whole_witness`: `checkObj` accepts the whole function, whose LL/SC loop reads `R27`
  across Progs (`CBNZ R27` after `STLXRW`): it relies on `X27` (`Tab.ok27`) exactly there, where
  `X27At` (`Sim.lean`) asks the machine's `X27` to be P0's (`docs/plans/proofs3.md` §7).
* `objAtomic_ldadd_run`, `objAtomic_stlxr_run`, `objAtomic_cas_hit`, `objAtomic_cas_miss`:
  `symInsn_sound` on the decoded words from concrete states: `LDADDAL` adds 5 to the 37 in memory
  and returns 37, `STLXR` stores and writes 0 to `W27`, `CASAL` stores on a match and leaves the
  memory alone on a mismatch, `W27` receiving the old value in both cases. The P0 Prog
  `CASALW R27, (R0), R2` has the same symbolic effect as its word (`casP`, `σCas`).
-/

